    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>New package comfyui for openSUSE:Factory from science:machinelearning (ComfyUI cone). pluskalm is the science:machinelearning package maintainer.

Requires python-av &gt;= 16 (Factory is 14.2.0 until sr#1372737). python-comfy-angle is Recommends only and is not packaged (prebuilt Electron libEGL/libGLESv2).

INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together (ComfyUI cone):
  * sr#1372780 python-trampoline
  * sr#1372737 python-av (devel:languages:python; Factory 14.2.0, need &gt;= 16 for comfyui)
  * remaining cone packages from science:machinelearning being submitted in this batch

Fri Aug 21 09:01:47 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal &lt;mpluskal@suse.com&gt;

- Initial package of ComfyUI 0.33.3: node-graph engine for local
  image, video, audio and 3D generation
  * Single-flavour application: tree in /usr/share/comfyui,
    launcher /usr/bin/comfyui
  * Launcher defaults --base-directory and --database-url to
    $XDG_DATA_HOME/comfyui (or ~/.local/share/comfyui)
  * Already includes the 0.28.0 security fixes:
    CVE-2026-56670, CVE-2026-56671, CVE-2026-56672, CVE-2026-56673
</comment>
    <requestid>1372800</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>f130a4f7c763cde2239aeb759b0e2cc4</srcmd5>
    <version>0.33.3</version>
    <time>1787427337</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>- Fix the very first start of comfyui aborting with a
  FileNotFoundError instead of serving the web UI: add
  comfyui-create-custom-nodes-directory.patch, which creates the
  custom_nodes directory in the per-user base directory
- Load the custom nodes shipped with ComfyUI again: the per-user
  base directory had hidden them, so SaveImageWebsocket, used by
  the packaged websocket API example, was unavailable
- Do not create the per-user directory tree for comfyui --help
- Require python-comfyui-frontend-package 1.50.6 (XSS fixes
  GHSA-2gr5-vw2p-2hcf, GHSA-j6xv-rx8r-mh6j, GHSA-8xxc-66vh-2pf3)

Supersedes sr#1373017, which carried only the Requires bump.

The FileNotFoundError is already live in Factory (comfyui-0.33.3-2.1):
os.listdir() on a per-user custom_nodes directory that nothing creates,
so every first-time user hits it on first start and it does not
self-heal. Fixed in folder_paths.py rather than the launcher so that
--base-directory and direct main.py invocations are covered too.

INTERDEPENDENT: please stage together with
python-comfyui-frontend-package 1.50.6 (sr#1373016). ComfyUI 0.33.3
pinned the frontend at 1.49.6; Factory cannot replace that RPM without
this Requires bump. sr#1373016 is currently in
openSUSE:Factory:Staging:adi:28 and needs to be re-paired with this
request.</comment>
    <requestid>1373109</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="3">
    <srcmd5>7cc77b3eb32e94613ad07d8acd7a07fa</srcmd5>
    <version>0.33.3</version>
    <time>1787579030</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Start on the CPU when no accelerator is present

comfy/model_management.py assumes a GPU unless --cpu is passed: cpu_state
is set to GPU at import and only args.cpu ever sets it back. On a
CPU-only machine the module level

  total_vram = get_total_memory(get_torch_device())

then raises &quot;AssertionError: Torch not compiled with CUDA enabled&quot; while
ComfyUI is still importing, so the server never starts. Factory builds
PyTorch without CUDA and without ROCm, so this is what every user gets
unless they know about --cpu.

Patch1 falls back to the CPU device when none of the accelerator
backends the module already probes is available. It logs a warning
rather than an informational line on purpose: the same condition holds
for a GPU-capable PyTorch whose device is momentarily unusable, and a
silent CPU run there would be far slower than expected.

Also bumps the exact python-comfy-aimdo requirement to 0.4.14 to match
request 1373273, so the pin keeps resolving when that lands.

Verified by running the built rpm, since neither the ComfyUI nor the
comfy-aimdo %check reaches this code: in an x86_64 container with the
Factory CPU-only torch, a flagless start from a clean home now reaches
&quot;Starting server&quot; instead of exiting 1.</comment>
    <requestid>1373274</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="4">
    <srcmd5>27f33d1ce207045581ca39306277f679</srcmd5>
    <version>0.33.3</version>
    <time>1787766808</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>comfyui carries exact &quot;=&quot; pins on the comfy* packages, which makes it
uninstallable the moment any one of them is updated on its own. That has
now happened: the pin is comfyui-workflow-templates = 0.11.44 and Factory
has accepted 0.11.46, so the dependency loses its provider as soon as that
build publishes.

Upstream's requirements.txt uses &quot;==&quot; for all of these, but upstream's own
check_comfy_packages_versions() (app/frontend_management.py) warns only
when the installed version is BELOW the required one, so upstream treats
them as floors. This converts all of them to floors.

No upper bounds are set. comfy-aimdo and comfy-kitchen are both imported
at module scope, so an API removal in either would fail at import time,
but no such break is known: the one comfy-kitchen minor bump so far
(0.1 -&gt; 0.2) removed no exported names, 0.2.0 -&gt; 0.2.31 only added them,
and comfy-aimdo's Python tree is byte-identical between 0.4.13 and 0.4.15.
A speculative cap would simply recreate the unresolvable state these
floors exist to fix. A real break gets a bound then, with the evidence.

The comfyui-frontend-package floor of 1.50.6 is a security floor rather
than a compatibility pin: it carries the fixes for GHSA-2gr5-vw2p-2hcf,
GHSA-j6xv-rx8r-mh6j and GHSA-8xxc-66vh-2pf3 (repo-level advisories on
Comfy-Org/ComfyUI_frontend, all High, patched in 1.50.2/1.50.4/1.50.5).
None of them has a CVE id, and openSUSE Bugzilla has no bug for either
package, so there is no boo# to cite.

comfy-aimdo's floor moves down from = 0.4.14 to upstream's declared
&gt;= 0.4.13; the 0.4.14 was tracking whatever happened to be packaged
rather than a real requirement.

Supersedes sr#1373685, which relaxed three of the four pins and left
comfy-kitchen exact.

Verified: native aarch64 build green, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 badness,
source_validator clean. The built RPM's requires resolve against what
Factory ships today (aimdo 0.4.14, kitchen 0.2.31, embedded-docs 0.5.10,
frontend 1.50.6, workflow-templates 0.11.46).</comment>
    <requestid>1373695</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>a4c1c63192006f632a21a93d08ea0d33</srcmd5>
    <version>0.34.0</version>
    <time>1787849590</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update comfyui to 0.34.0.

New model support (Pixal3d, TRELLIS2, Sam3d-body, taeh3), a large
MiniMax-H3 feature round, HDR/AV1/mkv/webm video writing, and fixes
for the default database path under a custom user directory and for
temp-directory asset previews.

0.34.1 exists as a git tag but has no published release, so 0.34.0
is what is submitted.

Upstream raised several runtime minimums. They are encoded here as
floors, deliberately not as the exact &quot;==&quot; pins requirements.txt
writes, because exact pins on the independently released comfy*
companion packages previously made comfyui uninstallable in Factory:

  python-av                         &gt;= 17.0.0 (was 16.0.0)
  python-comfy-aimdo                &gt;= 0.4.15 (was 0.4.13)
  python-comfyui-embedded-docs      &gt;= 0.5.10 (was 0.5.9)
  python-comfyui-workflow-templates &gt;= 0.11.48 (was 0.11.44)

All four are already at or above those versions in Factory, so the
package stays resolvable and this request needs no staging partner.

The python-comfyui-frontend-package floor deliberately stays at
&gt;= 1.50.6. The shipped v0.34.0 tarball asks for 1.49.6 (the 1.51.9
pin is on upstream master, not on this release), and 1.50.6 already
satisfies that while also being the security floor for the XSS fixes
GHSA-2gr5-vw2p-2hcf, GHSA-j6xv-rx8r-mh6j and GHSA-8xxc-66vh-2pf3.
Raising it to 1.51.9 would couple this request to the in-flight
python-comfyui-frontend-package submission for no benefit.

0.34.0 adds one new optional runtime dependency, picked up as
Recommends: python-numba, used by the new comfy_extras/mesh3d UV
unwrapping code when it is importable, with a working torch fallback
when it is not.

Both downstream patches (custom_nodes bootstrap under
--base-directory, CPU fallback when no accelerator is present) are
still required and apply unchanged; both are reported upstream.

Built locally for openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64, rpmlint unchanged
from the previous version.</comment>
    <requestid>1373929</requestid>
  </revision>
